WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.760
Give a guinea pig radioactive leucine, then look at its pancreas.

2
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:14.820
Within about five minutes, the newly made digestive enzymes sit over the rough

3
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.360
endoplasmic reticulum.

4
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.360
By about 20 minutes, the label lies over the Golgi.

5
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.780
By an hour, it is in the granules the cell will later release.

6
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.500
How do we know that order, and how fast does the protein move?

7
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.890
The method is called pulse-chase.

8
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.410
First comes a short pulse of radioactive amino acid.

9
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.130
Then comes the chase, a flood of unlabelled amino acid.

10
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.630
Now only protein made during the pulse carries label.

11
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.310
That labelled group is a cohort, and you follow it as it moves.

12
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:57.590
In the ER lumen, a core of 14 sugars is attached to the protein.

13
00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:02.870
It passes the ERGIC and enters the Golgi at the cis face.

14
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.910
Golgi enzymes then rebuild the sugar chain as the protein crosses to the trans side.

15
00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:14.810
Early enzymes act first, and galactose and sialic acid are added later.

16
00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.150
So the chain carries a stamp of how far the protein has come.

17
00:01:20.923 --> 00:01:25.043
Endoglycosidase H, or Endo H, reads that stamp.

18
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:27.543
It cuts high-mannose chains.

19
00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:33.323
It does not cut the complex chains made after the early Golgi enzymes have acted.

20
00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:36.643
Cut protein runs faster on a gel.

21
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:41.043
So the resistant band counts protein that has reached those enzymes.

22
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.347
Here is an illustrative time course.

23
00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:48.727
At each chase time, the two bands add up to 1,000.

24
00:01:49.307 --> 00:01:53.400
So the resistant share is 0, 33, 55, and 80 percent.

25
00:01:53.660 --> 00:02:03.200
The rate constant, k, comes out near 0.0267 per minute at 15, 30, and 60 minutes.

26
00:02:05.487 --> 00:02:08.487
The three agree, so one first-order step fits.

27
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:15.677
Half-time is 0.693 divided by k, or 26 minutes.

28
00:02:16.557 --> 00:02:20.457
That covers ER exit plus the trip to the Golgi enzymes.

29
00:02:20.897 --> 00:02:23.877
So it is an upper bound for ER exit alone.

30
00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:29.997
Resistance is a threshold in a sequence, not a switch between two organelles.

31
00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:35.197
Keep the rule: the sugar chain records how far the protein has come.
